Here I have collected various papers written by Vukan R. Vuchic, a professor of Transportation Systems at the University of Pennsylvania, which are relevant to improving transit, especially focusing on suburban railways and integration between different modes and different services.

#link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/person/81a2f158-5e5d-4d6c-b809-d103dbc99a20")[All papers]

= General principles
- #link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/publication/5aa49c43-9500-490d-863d-2b19aabb3228")[Theory and Practice of Metro Network Design]
- #link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/publication/006e7ff4-7e56-49aa-bc34-54b37847ee99")[Role and Organization of Transfers in Transit Networks]
- #link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/publication/cce83171-9521-43ea-97c5-13af752b938c")[Timed Transfer System Planning, Design and Operation]
- #link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/publication/f7661c62-604d-4ac0-b90f-d007859ed6f4")[From Suburban Railways to Regional Rail Systems]
- #link("https://repository.upenn.edu/entities/publication/136a56a4-cfce-419a-90c2-7340972f0587")[Transit Federation -- A Solution for Service Integration]

there's a lot more, but these seem to be the most relevant to us

